 "delivered": [
  "StageDeployment.published_proposal now reads the COMMITTED publication through driver.publication_for_attempt instead of re-composing the proposal manifest through retain_proposal, so a second Job's already published proposal is nameable after the first Job's integration moved the canonical target",
  "the obsolete two-Job expectation that recorded that blocker is replaced by test_the_second_jobs_published_proposal_survives_the_advance, which proves the historical proposal is readable, is the one Job B actually published, still names the base its line was declared at, and belongs to Job B's own Work -- while the immutable declared base and the moved target, which are what a reconciliation exists for, stay measured"
 ],
 "remaining": [
  "Integration._run must take the RECONCILED branch when the producer proposal's target is no longer the Authority's canonical one: P's prepare_result, record_causal_observations, publish_result, the three configured owners' receipts on the derived proposal, and record_result_evidence, then Q's driver.admit_authorized_result",
  "a configured verify_imported owner in stage_execution that runs the deployment's OWN required-test argv (Integration.required_tests) against the imported target commit and returns the closed execution.POST_IMPORT_MEMBERS document",
  "the deployment document must carry the dedicated target repository and the integration role's private workspace; _MEMBERS is closed and lives in stage_execution.py, so this is inside R's own paths",
  "Integration.account must accept the reconciled settlement's verification shape (verification.post_import_tests, whose command is text) beside the direct path's argv shape",
  "delegation.py's closed completion vocabulary must carry the original submission AND the derived integration receipt",
  "the actual A-then-B two-terminal witness on one target, with both changes, B's producer line/proposal/receipts unchanged, and finished capacity released"
 ],
 "tree_facts_established_this_claim": {
  "port_carries_the_git_facts": "tools/integration_worker.py's IntegrationRuntimePort already holds object_runner (public), _target_place and _storage -- but integration_worker.py is NOT in R's allowlist and those two are private-named, so the target repository and private workspace must reach the stage through the deployment document instead, which stage_execution.py owns",
  "settlement_shape_differs": "Integration.account compares entry['settlement']['verification']['argv'] against required_tests; the reconciled settlement Q writes carries verification.post_import_tests with a text command and no argv"
 },
